    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nThe `riskFlag` is a derived field on the owner response, true when **any** of the three signals holds. I added it as a small, self-contained unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n1. **New helper `OwnerRiskFlag.java`** \u2014 a static `of(Owner)` that ORs the three conditions, mirroring the existing `OwnerSegment`/`OwnerLocality` helper idiom:\n   - **possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (set by `FlagPossibleDuplicate`)\n   - **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` (set by `EnsureCityCapacity` at the 40-owner soft threshold below the hard cap of 50)\n   - **email domain disposable-adjacent** \u2192 the domain's registrable base label matches a known disposable provider (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) under any TLD or subdomain (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `inbox.mailinator.com`). The exact disposable domains are already 400-rejected at create by `RejectDisposableEmail`, so this catches the look-alikes that get persisted.\n\n2. **One `@Mapping` line** in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` calling `OwnerRiskFlag.of(owner)` \u2014 same expression style as the surrounding mappings.\n\n3. **`riskFlag` property** added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (readOnly boolean), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\nThe behaviour lives in a brand-new cohesive class with near-zero surrounding complexity, so the expensive `WMC_other` lever is untouched. The only *changed* existing function is `toOwnerDto` (CC 1, one added annotation line); the large `Owner`/`EnsureCityCapacity`/etc. classes were read but not edited. Three files touched total.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`) passes: a unique, email-less, low-population owner trips none of the signals, so `riskFlag` is `false`.",
